"Investment Spending Shock Analysis for Georgia",
,
Overview,
"This workbook analyzes the macroeconomic impact of a $6.5 billion USD investment in Georgia",
"over an 8-year period (2026-2033) using the macro accounting framework (demand side).",
,
"Investment Details",
"Total Investment:","6,500 million USD"
"Investment Period:","2026-2033 (8 years)"
"Exchange Rate:","2.746 GEL/USD"
"Total Investment (GEL):",17849
,
"Sheet Descriptions",
WEO_Data,"IMF World Economic Outlook data for Georgia (2020-2043). Contains GDP growth, nominal GDP, deflator, and inflation data."
"SUPPLY (38-38)-2024","Supply table from Georgia National Statistics Office (Geostat) for 2024. Shows production and imports by 38 product categories."
"USE (38-38)-2024","Use table from Geostat for 2024. Shows consumption, investment, exports by 38 product categories."
"SUT Calc","Calculations based on Supply and Use Tables. Links data from SUPPLY and USE sheets and calculates the import content share."
NA,"Baseline Scenario - National Accounts impact analysis with demand multiplier = 0.8 and import content from SUT."
NA_Scenario2,"Scenario 2 - Same as baseline but with demand multiplier = 1.0 (higher domestic demand effect)."
NA_Scenario3,"Scenario 3 - Same as baseline but with import content share = 0.5 (50% import content assumption)."
,
,
"Key Assumptions",
"Exchange Rate:","2.746 GEL/USD (fixed)"
"Demand Multiplier (Baseline):","0.8 (small open economy assumption)"
"Demand Multiplier (Scenario 2):",1.0
"Import Content (Baseline):","Calculated from SUT tables (actual data)"
"Import Content (Scenario 3):","0.5 (50% assumption)"
"Investment Allocation:","Bell-shaped: 5%, 10%, 15%, 20%, 20%, 15%, 10%, 5% over 8 years"
"GDP Growth (2027+):","5.5% (constant, as per IMF WEO projection)"
"Deflator Growth (2025+):","Average of 2021-2024 (fixed anchor)"
,
,
"Data Sources",
"1. IMF World Economic Outlook (October 2025)",
"2. National Statistics Office of Georgia (Geostat) - Supply and Use Tables 2024",
"   https://www.geostat.ge/en/modules/categories/632/supply-and-use-tables-new",
,
Methodology,
"The analysis follows the macro accounting framework (demand side):",
"1. Total investment is allocated over 8 years in a bell-shaped pattern",
"2. Investment is split into domestic content and import content",
"3. Domestic content generates demand effect = Domestic Content × Demand Multiplier",
"4. GDP impact is calculated as the demand effect as % of real GDP",
"5. All values are adjusted for inflation using GDP deflator",
